    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d408-a2">

                <pb facs="0743" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg647"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 479.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister of foreign affairs
                        to Mr. De Long.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office, Tokei</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            ana="#date_conversion-issue-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1873-09-20">20<hi rendition="#italic">th of
                                Ninth month of</hi> 6<hi rendition="#italic">th year,
                            Muyi</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your dispatch bearing date of the 25th of May, 1873, and stating
                    that Ytgana Ito had been arrested at Nagasaki. In reply I have to state that,
                    upon inquiries made of the proper authorities on the subject, I found that he
                    had been already released.</p>
                <p>With respect and consideration,</p>
                <closer><signed>SAYESHMIA TONEOMI,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">His Imperial Japanese
                            Majesty’s Minister for Foreign Affairs.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. E. De Long</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary of
                            United States of America in Japan.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
